# Authentication

## Token mechanism

| Piece | Where it lives in the frontend | Usage |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Access token (JWT, TTL 15 min) | Redux `state.auth.accessToken` — in memory only | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every protected request |
| Refresh token (TTL 48 h from login) | `httpOnly` cookie managed by the browser | Only `POST /auth/refresh` and `DELETE /auth/logout` |

The JWT is **not** renewed on every request — only on login and refresh.  
The `sameSite: strict` cookie requires the frontend origin to be in the backend's `CORS_ORIGIN` with `credentials: true`.

## Flow

1. User submits credentials → `auth.service.ts` calls `POST /api/auth/login`.
2. Backend responds `201` with `{ accessToken, admin: {...} }` and sets the `refresh_token` cookie.
3. Frontend stores the `accessToken` in Redux (`authSlice`) — **never in `localStorage`**.
4. The Axios interceptor attaches the access token to every request automatically.
5. On **401**, the interceptor silently calls `POST /api/auth/refresh` (cookie sent automatically) and retries the original request with the new token.
6. If refresh also returns 401 → dispatch `clearAuth()`, redirect to `/login`.
7. Logout: `DELETE /api/auth/logout` — requires Bearer **and** cookie; the backend clears the whitelist and removes the cookie.

## Auth service

```typescript
// apps/admin/src/modules/auth/services/auth.service.ts
import { apiClient } from "@/lib/api/api-client";
import type { IApiResponse } from "@repo/lib/api/api-response.types";
import type { ILoginPayload, IAuthAdmin } from "../types/auth.types";

export async function login(
  payload: ILoginPayload,
): Promise<{ accessToken: string; admin: IAuthAdmin }> {
  const { data } = await apiClient.post<
    IApiResponse<{ accessToken: string; admin: IAuthAdmin }>
  >("/auth/login", payload);
  return data.data;
}

export async function logout(): Promise<void> {
  // DELETE — requires Bearer (attached by the interceptor) + httpOnly cookie
  await apiClient.delete("/auth/logout");
}
```

## useAuth hook

```typescript
// apps/admin/src/modules/auth/hooks/use-auth.ts
"use client";

import { useRouter } from "next/navigation";
import { useAppDispatch, useAppSelector } from "@/store/hooks";
import { setAuth, clearAuth } from "@/store/slices/auth.slice";
import { login, logout } from "../services/auth.service";
import type { ILoginPayload } from "../types/auth.types";
import { ROUTES } from "@/lib/constants/routes.constants";

export function useAuth(): {
  user: IAuthAdmin | null;
  isAuthenticated: boolean;
  login: (payload: ILoginPayload) => Promise<void>;
  logout: () => Promise<void>;
} {
  const dispatch = useAppDispatch();
  const router = useRouter();
  const user = useAppSelector((state) => state.auth.user);
  const isAuthenticated = useAppSelector((state) => state.auth.isAuthenticated);

  const handleLogin = async (payload: ILoginPayload): Promise<void> => {
    const { accessToken, admin } = await login(payload);
    dispatch(setAuth({ accessToken, user: admin }));
    router.push(ROUTES.admin.dashboard);
  };

  const handleLogout = async (): Promise<void> => {
    await logout();
    dispatch(clearAuth());
    router.push(ROUTES.login);
  };

  return { user, isAuthenticated, login: handleLogin, logout: handleLogout };
}
```

## Route guard — admin layout

The admin layout is the only place that enforces the guard. No individual page checks auth on its own.

```tsx
// apps/admin/src/app/(admin)/layout.tsx
"use client";

import { useEffect } from "react";
import { useRouter } from "next/navigation";
import { useAppSelector } from "@/store/hooks";
import { ROUTES } from "@/lib/constants/routes.constants";

export default function AdminLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}): React.JSX.Element {
  const isAuthenticated = useAppSelector((state) => state.auth.isAuthenticated);
  const router = useRouter();

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isAuthenticated) {
      router.replace(ROUTES.login);
    }
  }, [isAuthenticated, router]);

  if (!isAuthenticated) return <></>;

  return (
    <div className="flex h-screen">
      <Sidebar />
      <main className="flex-1 overflow-auto p-6">{children}</main>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Auth types

```typescript
// apps/admin/src/modules/auth/types/auth.types.ts

// Login uses username, not email
export interface ILoginPayload {
  username: string;
  password: string;
}

// Exact shape of the 'admin' object returned by the backend
export interface IAuthAdmin {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  lastName: string;
  username: string;
  email: string;
}

export interface IAuthTokens {
  accessToken: string;
  admin: IAuthAdmin;
}
```

## Rules

- The access token lives **only in Redux** (`state.auth.accessToken`) — never in `localStorage`, never in a JS-managed cookie.
- The refresh token is an `httpOnly` cookie — the frontend never reads or writes it directly.
- The login field is `username`, **not** `email`. The backend responds `401` with the same message whether the username or password is wrong.
- Logout is `DELETE /auth/logout` — requires the active Bearer plus the cookie; without Bearer the backend returns 401.
- Authentication is enforced at **layout level** (`app/(admin)/layout.tsx`), not page by page.
- The login page must be **outside** the `(admin)` route group to avoid the guard.
- `useAuth` is the only hook that dispatches auth actions — components never dispatch `setAuth` or `clearAuth` directly.
- This rule applies **exclusively** to `apps/admin/`. `apps/web` and `apps/blog` have no auth logic.
